<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<!--
	Universal Links (com.apple.developer.associated-domains) belong here too,
	once two things exist: the Apple Developer Program membership
	(CLIENT_REQUIREMENTS.md #2) so the App ID can have the Associated Domains
	capability enabled in the first place, and the real domain
	(CLIENT_REQUIREMENTS.md #5, config/deepLinkConfig.ts's APP_LINK_HOST)
	hosting /.well-known/apple-app-site-association over HTTPS. Deliberately
	not added yet: an entitlement Xcode can't match to an enabled capability
	on the signing account risks a local build failure, for a feature that
	can't function until both of those exist anyway. When ready, add:
		<key>com.apple.developer.associated-domains</key>
		<array>
			<string>applinks:lifefull.app</string>
		</array>
	(matching APP_LINK_HOST exactly) and enable the capability on the App ID
	in the Apple Developer portal first.
-->
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.developer.applesignin</key>
	<array>
		<string>Default</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
